  "result": "The refusals for a revoked, already-used or expired invitation are all in `acceptInvitation` in `src/server/services/invitation-service.ts`. It looks the invitation up by token hash, then throws one of three errors:\n- **Revoked:** \"That invitation has been revoked\".\n- **Already used:** \"That invitation has already been accepted\".\n- **Too old:** \"That invitation has expired\".\n\nThe setting that decides how old is too old is `DEFAULT_EXPIRY_DAYS = 14` in the same file. `inviteMembers` passes it as `expiresInDays` when it creates an invitation. `insertInvitation` in `src/server/repositories/invitation-repository.ts` then turns it into the stored `expiresAt` (now plus that many days). The accept check compares that stored `expiresAt` to the current time.\n\n`src/schemas/invitation.ts` also has a `expiresInDays` field (default 14, range 1–30). The invite service doesn't use that schema for this value, so the constant is what actually applies.\n\nANSWER: src/server/services/invitation-service.ts",
